# Development deployment

Provisioned Singapore hosting with infra/hosting.bicep, deployed the locally
verified image with infra/hosting-app.bicep, and created a separate GitHub OIDC
identity with infra/github-identity.bicep. Identifiers are recorded in
infra/azure-hosting.deployment.json. Both HTTPS health endpoints passed, including
PostgreSQL readiness. The testing GitHub environment has its Azure variables
and branch restriction configured. Production hosting is not provisioned.

CI runs application checks, PostgreSQL integration tests, and a Docker smoke test.
CD publishes the exact CI image to private ACR, deploys its digest, and verifies
the new Azure revision and HTTPS health. See CI_CD.md for prerequisites,
activation, migration handling, and rollback. Runtime credentials stay in Key
Vault and ignored local files.
